{# Resolve tool names from the active tool list (Anthropic-style or legacy). #}
{% set bash_tool = namespace.tools.get("bash_code_execution_tool_name")
    or namespace.tools.get("bash_tool_name") %}
{% set text_editor_tool = namespace.tools.get("text_editor_code_execution_tool_name")
    or namespace.tools.get("text_editor_tool_name") %}
{% set view_tool = namespace.tools.get("view_tool_name") %}
{% set str_replace_tool = namespace.tools.get("str_replace_tool_name") %}
{% set create_tool = namespace.tools.get("create_tool_name") %}
{% set insert_tool = namespace.tools.get("insert_tool_name") %}
{% set present_files_tool = namespace.tools.get("present_files_tool_name") %}
{% set present_server_tool = namespace.tools.get("present_server_tool_name") %}
{% set has_leaf_editor = view_tool or str_replace_tool or create_tool or insert_tool %}
{% set section_name = bash_tool or text_editor_tool or "code_execution" %}
{# Default: no internet (matches CodeExecutionSettings.internet_enabled default). #}
{% set internet_enabled = internet_enabled if internet_enabled is defined else false %}
{% set preinstalled_packages = preinstalled_packages if preinstalled_packages is defined else [] %}
{% set preinstalled_cli_tools = preinstalled_cli_tools if preinstalled_cli_tools is defined else [] %}

{% if layout is not defined or not layout %}{% else %}
{% set workspace = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "user") | first %}
{% set outputs = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "outputs") | first %}
{% set uploads = layout | selectattr("name", "equalto", "uploads") | first %}
<code_execution>
You have a sandboxed code execution environment.

**Available tools**
{% if bash_tool -%}
- `{{ bash_tool }}` — run shell commands (`command`)
{% endif -%}
{% if text_editor_tool -%}
- `{{ text_editor_tool }}` — read/edit text files via `command`: `view`, `str_replace`, `create`, or `insert` (plus `path` and the fields for that command)
{% elif has_leaf_editor -%}
- File tools:{% if view_tool %} `{{ view_tool }}` (read){% endif %}{% if str_replace_tool %}, `{{ str_replace_tool }}` (edit){% endif %}{% if create_tool %}, `{{ create_tool }}` (create){% endif %}{% if insert_tool %}, `{{ insert_tool }}` (insert){% endif %}
{% endif -%}
{% if present_files_tool -%}
- `{{ present_files_tool }}` — **required** to show files to the user (`filepaths`: absolute paths). Writing a file does not surface it in chat.
{% endif -%}
{% if present_server_tool -%}
- `{{ present_server_tool }}` — **required** to expose a sandbox HTTP service (`port`; optional `service_name`, `initial_path`)
{% endif %}
{% if preinstalled_packages or preinstalled_cli_tools %}

**Environment**
{% if preinstalled_packages -%}
- Preinstalled Python packages: {{ preinstalled_packages | join(", ") }}
{% endif -%}
{% if preinstalled_cli_tools -%}
- Preinstalled CLI tools: {{ preinstalled_cli_tools | join(", ") }}
{% endif -%}
{% endif %}

**Filesystem**
| Path | Access | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{% for mount in layout -%}
| `{{ mount.target }}` | {{ mount.access }} | {{ mount.description }} |
{% endfor %}

**Rules**
- Use absolute paths. Working directory: `{{ workspace.target }}`.
- Stay inside the paths above.
- Put intermediate work and scripts in `{{ workspace.target }}`. Put final user deliverables in `{{ outputs.target }}`.
- Prefer writing code to a file under `{{ workspace.target }}`, then running that file{% if bash_tool %} with `{{ bash_tool }}`{% endif %}. Avoid long one-off inline code in the shell so failures are easy to inspect and fix with edits.
{% if text_editor_tool or has_leaf_editor -%}
- Prefer the text-editor tool(s) to create/edit those files; use {% if bash_tool %}`{{ bash_tool }}`{% else %}the shell{% endif %} to run them, and for installs/non-text work.
{% endif -%}
{% if not internet_enabled -%}
- No internet: outbound network is disabled. Do not use `pip install`, `npm install`, `curl`, `wget`, `apt`, or any other download/install that needs the network. Use only the preinstalled packages/CLI tools listed above and local files.
{% endif -%}
{% if present_files_tool -%}
- After creating/updating deliverables, call `{{ present_files_tool }}` with their absolute paths (batch when possible). Do not claim a file is downloadable unless you already presented it.
{% endif -%}
{% if present_server_tool -%}
- After starting an HTTP server in the sandbox, call `{{ present_server_tool }}` with its port.
{% endif -%}
{% if few_shots == "True" %}

**Examples**
{% if bash_tool -%}
- Read upload: `{{ bash_tool }}` → `command="cat {{ uploads.target }}report.csv"`
{% endif -%}
{% if text_editor_tool and bash_tool -%}
- Write then run: `{{ text_editor_tool }}` → `command="create"`, `path="{{ workspace.target }}analyze.py"`, `file_text="..."`; then `{{ bash_tool }}` → `command="python {{ workspace.target }}analyze.py"`
- On failure: edit the file with `{{ text_editor_tool }}` (`command="str_replace"`) and re-run
{% elif bash_tool -%}
- Write then run a script under `{{ workspace.target }}`, edit it if it fails, then re-run
{% endif -%}
{% if bash_tool -%}
- Write output: `{{ bash_tool }}` → `command="cp chart.png {{ outputs.target }}chart.png"`
{% endif -%}
{% if present_files_tool -%}
- Show to user: `{{ present_files_tool }}` → `filepaths=["{{ outputs.target }}chart.png"]`
{% endif -%}
{% if present_server_tool -%}
- Expose app: `{{ present_server_tool }}` → `port=8501`
{% endif -%}
{% endif %}
</code_execution>
{% endif %}
